Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: keep the DV VSIF exclusive on CachyOS

CachyOS 7.2 moves the HDMI 1.4 VSIF from vsp_infopacket to hfvsif_infopacket.
On upstream 7.2 the DV VSIF overwrote it; invalidate the separate slot while
DV Standard is active so the sink receives only the Dolby VSIF, as tested.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_dv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_dv.c
index 11a3a27..fb01a36 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_dv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_dv.c
@@ -263,6 +263,10 @@ int amdgpu_dm_dv_configure_stream(struct dc_stream_state *stream,
 	/* Publish the candidate only after every packet has been prepared. */
 	stream->avi_infopacket = avi_packet;
 	stream->vsp_infopacket = vsp_packet;
+	/* CachyOS sends the HDMI 1.4 VSIF from its own slot; upstream 7.2 shared
+	 * vsp_infopacket, so the DV VSIF replaced it. Keep the DV VSIF the only one.
+	 */
+	stream->hfvsif_infopacket.valid = false;
 	stream->dv_standard = true;
 	stream->timing.hdmi_vic = caps.legacy_vsif ? legacy.vic : 0;
 	stream->timing.vic = avi.video_code;
